ms: flex-start; margin: 20px 0;\" data-mce-style=\"display: flex; align-items: flex-start; margin: 20px 0;\"><img style=\"width: 120px; flex-shrink: 0; margin-right: 20px;\" src=\"./images/system-design-139-img-15.png\" alt=\"Document Model\" data-mce-src=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251223163308873853/Scalable-Distributed-Systems.png\" data-mce-style=\"width: 120px; flex-shrink: 0; margin-right: 20px;\"><div style=\"flex: 1;\" data-mce-style=\"flex: 1;\"><strong>Scalable Distributed Systems</strong><br>Load balancing using L4 and L7 balancers, sharding, and replication strategies.</div></div><div style=\"display: flex; align-items: flex-start; margin: 20px 0;\" data-mce-style=\"display: flex; align-items: flex-start; margin: 20px 0;\"><img style=\"width: 120px; flex-shrink: 0; margin-right: 20px;\" src=\"./images/system-design-139-img-16.png\" alt=\"Document Model\" data-mce-src=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251223163308863300/Infrastructure-Pipelines.png\" data-mce-style=\"width: 120px; flex-shrink: 0; margin-right: 20px;\"><div style=\"flex: 1;\" data-mce-style=\"flex: 1;\"><strong>Infrastructure Pipelines</strong><br>CI/CD systems with artifact storage, rollback strategies, and worker pools.</div></div><div style=\"display: flex; align-items: flex-start; margin: 20px 0;\" data-mce-style=\"display: flex; align-items: flex-start; margin: 20px 0;\"><img style=\"width: 120px; flex-shrink: 0; margin-right: 20px;\" src=\"./images/system-design-139-img-17.png\" alt=\"Document Model\" data-mce-src=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251223163308853770/Concurrency-Basics.png\" data-mce-style=\"width: 120px; flex-shrink: 0; margin-right: 20px;\"><div style=\"flex: 1;\" data-mce-style=\"flex: 1;\"><strong>Concurrency &amp; Scalability</strong><span id=\"mce_marker\" data-mce-type=\"bookmark\" data-mce-fragment=\"1\"></span><br>Concurrency concepts, including concurrent request handling, async processing, and distributed task coordination.<span id=\"mce_marker\" data-mce-type=\"bookmark\" data-mce-fragment=\"1\"></span><br></div></div><div style=\"display: flex; align-items: flex-start; margin: 20px 0;\" data-mce-style=\"display: flex; align-items: flex-start; margin: 20px 0;\"><img style=\"width: 120px; flex-shrink: 0; margin-right: 20px;\" src=\"./images/system-design-139-img-18.png\" alt=\"Document Model\" data-mce-src=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251223163308843384/API-Production-Design.png\" data-mce-style=\"width: 120px; flex-shrink: 0; margin-right: 20px;\"><div style=\"flex: 1;\" data-mce-style=\"flex: 1;\"><strong>API Production Design</strong><br>API layer design with proper error handling and validation.</div></div></div><div class=\"courseOverview_msg_action__mgjUm courses_overview_read_more\"><span>Read <!-- -->more </span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;display:inline-block;overflow:hidden;width:initial;height:initial;background:none;opacity:1;border:0;margin:0;padding:0;position:relative;max-width:100%\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;display:block;width:initial;height:initial;background:none;opacity:1;border:0;margin:0;padding:0;max-width:100%\"><img style=\"display:block;max-width:100%;width:initial;height:initial;background:none;opacity:1;border:0;margin:0;padding:0\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" src=\"./images/system-design-139-img-19.jpg\"></span><img src=\"./images/system-design-139-img-20.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" data-nimg=\"intrinsic\" style=\"position:absolute;top:0;left:0;bottom:0;right:0;box-sizing:border-box;padding:0;border:none;margin:auto;display:block;width:0;height:0;min-width:100%;max-width:100%;min-height:100%;max-height:100%\"><noscript><img srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/img-practice/prod/courses/6/Web/Content/double%20arrow%20down_1712668255.svg 1x, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/img-practice/prod/courses/6/Web/Content/double%20arrow%20down_1712668255.svg 2x\" src=\"./images/system-design-139-img-21.svg\" decoding=\"async\" data-nimg=\"intrinsic\" style=\"position:absolute;top:0;left:0;bottom:0;right:0;box-sizing:border-box;padding:0;border:none;margin:auto;display:block;width:0;height:0;min-width:100%;max-width:100%;min-height:100%;max-height:100%\" loading=\"lazy\"></noscript></span></div></div></div></section><section class=\"whatGfgHavetoOffer_container__BvV0u\"><div class=\"col-11 col-sm-9 col-lg-9 mx-auto whatGfgHavetoOffer_course_feature_web__K4UII\"><h2 class=\"whatGfgHavetoOffer_heading__ITx5l\">What Sets Us Apart</h2><div class=\"whatGfgHavetoOffer_course_feature_cards_container__xnCfI\"><div class=\"whatGfgHavetoOffer_course_feature_card___6ZEH\"><div class=\"whatGfgHavetoOffer_course_feature_card_thumbnail__tfBpm\"><img height=\"60\" width=\"60\" src=\"./images/system-design-139-img-22.png\" alt=\"Recognised Certification\"></div><div class=\"whatGfgHavetoOffer_course_feature_card_content__qJ4kY\"><h3 class=\"whatGfgHavetoOffer_course_feature_card_title__wDoq7\">Recognised Certification</h3><div class=\"whatGfgHavetoOffer_course_feature_card_desc__EChXT\">Earn an industry-recognized GeeksforGeeks Training Certificate for credible validation, career advancement, and lifetime</div></div></div><div class=\"whatGfgHavetoOffer_course_feature_card___6ZEH\"><div class=\"whatGfgHavetoOffer_course_feature_card_thumbnail__tfBpm\"><img height=\"60\" width=\"60\" src=\"./images/system-design-139-img-23.png\" alt=\"24 X 7 AI Doubt Support\"></div><div class=\"whatGfgHavetoOffer_course_feature_card_content__qJ4kY\"><h3 class=\"whatGfgHavetoOffer_course_feature_card_title__wDoq7\">24 X 7 AI Doubt Support</h3><div class=\"whatGfgHavetoOffer_course_feature_card_desc__EChXT\">AI Chat Support for instant doubt resolution, plus a dedicated Teaching Assistant exclusively assigned to your batch.</div></div></div><div class=\"whatGfgHavetoOffer_course_feature_card___6ZEH\"><div class=\"whatGfgHavetoOffer_course_feature_card_thumbnail__tfBpm\"><img height=\"60\" width=\"60\" src=\"./images/system-design-139-img-24.jpg\" alt=\"Modern AI Toolkit\"></div><div class=\"whatGfgHavetoOffer_course_feature_card_content__qJ4kY\"><h3 class=\"whatGfgHavetoOffer_course_feature_card_title__wDoq7\">Modern AI Toolkit</h3><div class=\"whatGfgHavetoOffer_course_feature_card_desc__EChXT\">Takes techies from AI tools to AI-native systems, covering prompts, RAG, agents, MCPs, and full-stack AI.</div></div></div></div></div></section><section class=\"coursesSlug_batches_content_container__YcqQF\"><h3 class=\"coursesSlug_heading__G_r2E\">Course Syllabus</h3><div class=\"coursesSlug_batches_names_container__XgTIt\"><div class=\"coursesSlug_batch_name__QaTCS active\">System Design Training Program</div><div class=\"coursesSlug_batch_name__QaTCS \">AI Toolkit for Developers</div></div><div style=\"display:block\" class=\"coursesSlug_tabs_content_container__gJL5_\"><div class=\"coursesSlug_batch_content_tab__eui8a\"><div class=\"coursesSlug_content_container__aYL71 \"><h3>Module 1: System Design Thinking &amp; Requirement Analysis</h3><div class=\"coursesSlug_content__5chLp\"><ul><li>What is HLD - scope, goals, functional vs non-functional requirements</li><li>PEDALS / RESHADED interview frameworks</li><li>Capacity estimation - DAU, QPS, storage back-of-envelope calculations</li><li>Bottleneck analysis and identifying system constraints</li><li>API contracts and interface design principles</li><li>Client-server architecture fundamentals</li><li>Trade-off decision framework (CAP, latency vs consistency)</li></ul><p><strong>Case Study:</strong> Bitly URL Shortener</p></div></div><div class=\"coursesSlug_content_container__aYL71 \"><h3>Module 2: Scalability Fundamentals</h3><div class=\"coursesSlug_content__5chLp\"><ul><li>Vertical vs horizontal scaling - trade-offs and use cases</li><li>Stateless architecture for horizontal scalability</li><li>Load balancing - round-robin, least connections, IP hash</li><li>Sticky sessions - challenges, failure modes, and alternatives</li><li>Auto-scaling fundamentals and scaling policies</li><li>Geographic distribution and multi-region deployments</li><li>Cost vs performance trade-offs</li></ul><p><strong>Case Study: </strong>Dropbox</p></div></div><div class=\"coursesSlug_content_container__aYL71 \"><h3>Module 3: Database Fundamentals</h3><div class=\"coursesSlug_content__5chLp\"><ul><li>RDBMS vs NoSQL - when to choose which</li><li>ACID properties and BASE model</li><li>CAP theorem and PACELC theorem</li><li>Database indexing strategies - B-tree, hash, composite indexes</li><li>Schema design and query optimization fundamentals</li><li>Database performance bottlenecks</li></ul><p><strong>Case Study:</strong> Local Delivery Service</p></div></div><div class=\"coursesSlug_content_container__aYL71 coursesSlug_border_unset__F6P9j\"><h3>Module 4: Database Scaling</h3><div class=\"coursesSlug_content__5chLp\"><ul><li>Database sharding - horizontal partitioning strategies</li><li>Consistent hashing for shard routing</li><li>Read/write separation - primary replica pattern</li><li>Read replicas and scaling read-heavy workloads</li><li>Multi-leader replication and conflict resolution</li><li>Connection pooling and database optimization</li></ul><p><strong>Case Study:</strong> News Aggregator</p></div></div><div class=\"coursesSlug_show_more_action__ADady\"><span>Read <!-- -->more</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;display:inline-block;overflow:hidden;width:initial;height:initial;background:none;opacity:1;border:0;margin:0;padding:0;position:relative;max-width:100%\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;display:block;width:initial;height:initial;background:none;opacity:1;border:0;margin:0;padding:0;max-width:100%\"><img style=\"display:block;max-width:100%;width:initial;height:initial;background:none;opacity:1;border:0;margin:0;padding:0\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" src=\"./images/system-design-139-img-25.jpg\"></span><img src=\"./images/system-design-139-img-26.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" data-nimg=\"intrinsic\" style=\"position:absolute;top:0;left:0;bottom:0;right:0;box-sizing:border-box;padding:0;border:none;margin:auto;display:block;width:0;height:0;min-width:100%;max-width:100%;min-height:100%;max-height:100%\"><noscript><img srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/img-practice/prod/courses/6/Web/Content/double%20arrow%20down_1712668255.svg 1x, https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/img-practice/prod/courses/6/Web/Content/double%20arrow%20down_1712668255.svg 2x\" src=\"./images/system-design-139-img-27.svg\" decoding=\"async\" data-nimg=\"intrinsic\" style=\"position:absolute;top:0;left:0;bottom:0;right:0;box-sizing:border-box;padding:0;border:none;margin:auto;display:block;width:0;height:0;min-width:100%;max-width:100%;min-height:100%;max-height:100%\" loading=\"lazy\"></noscript></span></div><div class=\"coursesSlug_courses_view_detailed_syllabus__aFDKy courses_view_detailed_syllabus\"><a class=\"login-modal-btn\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"genericActionButton_generic_btn__n9vXy login-modal-btn \">Login to View Brochure</button></a></div></div></div><div style=\"display:none\" class=\"coursesSlug_tabs_content_container__gJL5_\"><div class=\"coursesSlug_batch_content_tab__eui8a\"><div class=\"coursesSlug_content_container__aYL71 \"><h3>1: The AI Toolkit &amp; Developer Setup</h3><div class=\"coursesSlug_content__5chLp\"><ul><li>Map of AI tools: LLMs, code assistants, AI search, agents</li><li>Tool categories: chat models, IDE copilots, CLI agents</li><li>Evaluation framework: accuracy, context window, cost, latency</li><li>When AI helps vs. when it hurts: real limitations</li><li>Setting up an AI-powered dev environment in 30 minutes</li><li>Live experiment: solving the same problem with multiple tools</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"coursesSlug_content_container__aYL71 \"><h3>2: Prompt Engineering &amp; Vibe Coding</h3><div class=\"coursesSlug_content__5chLp\"><ul><li>Vibe coding: natural language to code (fast prototyping)</li><li>Anatomy of a developer prompt: role, context, task, constraints</li><li>Zero-shot to few-shot escalation strategy</li><li>Chain-of-thought prompting for better reasoning</li><li>Iterative prompting and fixing hallucinations</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"coursesSlug_content_container__aYL71 \"><h3>3: Spec-Driven Development with AI</h3><div class=\"coursesSlug_content__5chLp\"><ul><li>Transition from prompts to structured specifications</li><li>Writing clear technical specs before code generation</li><li>Few-shot prompting with real codebase patterns</li><li>Generating reliable code aligned with requirements</li><li>Reducing ambiguity and improving determinism</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"coursesSlug_content_container__aYL71 coursesSlug_border_unset__F6P9j\"><h3>4: RAG Systems &amp; Context-Aware AI</h3><div class=\"coursesSlug_content__5chLp\"><ul><li>Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) fundamentals</li><li>Embeddings, vector databases, semantic search</li><li>Connecting AI to codebases, docs, and internal data</li><li>Building developer assistants using RAG</li><li>Limitations and failure modes of RAG systems</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"coursesSlug_show_more_action__ADady\"><span>Read <!-- -->more</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;display:inline-block;overflow:hidden;width:initial;height:initial;background:none;opacity:1;border:0;margin:0;padding:0;position:relative;max-width:100%\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;display:block;width:initial;height:initial;background:none;opacity:1;border:0;margin:0;padding:0;max-width:100%\"><img style=\"display:block;max-width:100%;width:initial;height:initial;background:none;opacity:1;border:0;margin:0;padding:0\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" src=\"./images/system-design-139-img-28.jpg\"></span><img src=\"./images/system-design-139-img-29.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" data-nimg=\"intrinsic\" style=\"position:absolute;top:0;left:0;bottom:0;right:0;box-sizing:border-box;padding:0;border:none;margin:auto